From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:46:09 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: add a probe-only driver for the scaler/CSC
 engine

Every Apple silicon SoC has one or more MSR engines: memory-to-memory
scalers with a programmable colour-space converter, chroma resampling,
flip/rotate and alpha fill. macOS reaches them through IOSurfaceAccelerator
and VideoToolbox; Linux has had no driver, so scaling and YUV/RGB
conversion fall back to the CPU or GPU.

Hardware-version 10 (M1) through 22 (A18 Pro) program the engine through
MMIO and signal completion with an interrupt. This first step binds the
existing apple,scaler nodes for T6041 (M4 Pro/Max) and T8140 (A18 Pro):
it attaches the MSR power domains with runtime-PM links, requires the
DART, reads the identity and idle state, clears and masks the interrupt
and keeps the engine idle. The video device and job submission follow
once the RGB path is qualified on hardware.

The DT nodes stay disabled, so nothing changes on existing systems.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 78512ff8850635ea5d3a51eca32eed3432e85a03)
[j604: Kconfig/Makefile context: no ave/ or prores/ in this base, only the scaler/ lines are added]
